      "content": "Taking propranolol without a prescription is dangerous, especially since it is a prescription medication specifically indicated for high blood pressure and other heart conditions rather than stage fright. Because you have a history of asthma, beta-blockers like propranolol can unexpectedly trigger severe attacks or breathing issues, which contradicts your assessment that you are currently fine. It is far safer to focus on non-pharmacological techniques, such as drinking water, deep breathing exercises, or practicing grounding methods, to manage the physical symptoms today. Please consult your healthcare provider immediately for any medical decision regarding your health and current medications.",
